WEBVTT

00:02.280 --> 00:05.477
- Hey.
- Hey, what are you doing home?

00:05.640 --> 00:08.234
Linda's spending time
with her son tonight.

00:08.400 --> 00:12.439
Apparently she's one of those
single moms that puts her kid first.

00:13.080 --> 00:14.593
The bitch.

00:17.120 --> 00:20.032
You're just saying that
because our mom put us third.

00:20.200 --> 00:23.476
Fourth after she got the Datsun 280Z.

00:23.640 --> 00:25.995
So, what you doing?

00:26.160 --> 00:28.515
Paying our household bills.

00:28.680 --> 00:30.511
You're a good wife, Alan.

00:32.360 --> 00:35.238
I can't believe some lucky fella
hasn't snapped you up.

00:36.080 --> 00:38.435
Probably the penis.

00:39.760 --> 00:42.115
That's usually a deal breaker.

00:42.840 --> 00:45.274
So how are we doing, bill-wise?

00:45.440 --> 00:46.759
Not very well.

00:46.920 --> 00:49.718
Are you aware you haven't had
a paying job in over nine months?

00:49.880 --> 00:53.429
Are you aware
that urine cures athlete's foot?

00:58.080 --> 01:01.436
Seriously, you've got a big pile of bills
and no money coming in.

01:01.600 --> 01:04.433
Seriously, no burning,
no itching, just clears it right up.

01:05.800 --> 01:09.873
The drug companies don't want you
to know about it because it's free.

01:11.280 --> 01:12.918
Charlie, you're unemployed.

01:13.080 --> 01:16.914
I know. Haven't you heard?
The jingle business is dead.

01:17.080 --> 01:19.071
How would I hear that?
Who would have told me?

01:19.240 --> 01:21.151
It was in all the jingle magazines.

01:23.080 --> 01:24.957
You know,
before they went out of business.

01:26.600 --> 01:28.670
Everybody's using old rock songs now.

01:28.840 --> 01:31.400
They're not gonna hire me
to write a jingle for tampons...

01:31.560 --> 01:34.199
...when they can just play
"Stuck in the Middle With You."

01:38.920 --> 01:40.592
But...

01:41.000 --> 01:42.831
This doesn't concern you at all?

01:43.000 --> 01:45.673
- No, something will turn up.
- How can you be so sure?

01:45.840 --> 01:48.593
Hey, do you have any idea
how I got in the jingle business?

01:48.760 --> 01:50.830
- No.
- Neither do I.

01:52.120 --> 01:54.350
But look how good that worked out.

01:54.520 --> 01:57.159
Charlie, you cannot depend
on the kindness of the universe.

01:57.320 --> 01:58.309
I have to.

01:58.480 --> 02:00.755
I don't have an older brother
I can sponge off of.

02:02.760 --> 02:06.036
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I'm gonna go pee on my feet.

02:50.520 --> 02:52.238
Okay.

02:53.760 --> 02:55.398
Oh, crap.

02:57.400 --> 03:00.551
- Berta, you got a minute?
- What's on your mind, princess?

03:02.280 --> 03:03.474
Well, first and foremost...

03:03.640 --> 03:06.837
...you know that we consider you
a beloved member of this family.

03:07.000 --> 03:11.551
Alan, you can roll manure in powdered
sugar, but it still ain't a jelly doughnut.

03:14.120 --> 03:15.473
Now see, right there...

03:15.640 --> 03:18.438
...that's one of the things
that we love about you, you know.

03:18.600 --> 03:20.989
- Folksy...
- Spill it, Mildred.

03:21.160 --> 03:23.879
Right, right, well,
I'm not sure you're aware of this...

03:24.040 --> 03:28.033
...but it has been quite some time
since Charlie has had any actual income.

03:28.200 --> 03:29.679
Okay.

03:29.840 --> 03:31.353
And I can't help but notice...

03:31.520 --> 03:36.071
...that you're the only beloved
family member actually drawing a salary.

03:36.960 --> 03:38.996
I'm also the only
beloved family member...

03:39.160 --> 03:41.628
...who takes a toothbrush
to your kid's skivvies.

03:43.440 --> 03:47.069
And we can never begin
to repay you for that.

03:47.240 --> 03:51.233
But during these difficult financial times,
we all have...

03:51.400 --> 03:53.789
For the record,
it's not my toothbrush, right?

03:56.360 --> 03:59.238
Not right now,
but cut my pay and all bets are off.

03:59.400 --> 04:01.118
Oh, come on, Berta, be reasonable.

04:01.280 --> 04:04.033
This might be more than just
a temporary dry spell for Charlie.

04:04.200 --> 04:07.351
Look, I know
things may seem dark right now...

04:07.520 --> 04:10.159
...but I've known Charlie
a lot longer than you have.

04:10.320 --> 04:12.993
- Technically, that's not true.
- Are you gonna let me talk?

04:14.080 --> 04:15.069
Sorry.

04:15.240 --> 04:18.277
One thing I've learned
working for Mr. Charles Roscoe Harper...

04:18.440 --> 04:21.637
- His middle name isn't Roscoe.
- Who's telling the story?

04:23.160 --> 04:24.513
Continue.

04:24.680 --> 04:28.878
Anyway, what I've learned
is God takes care of drunks and fools.

04:29.040 --> 04:31.235
And C. Roscoe Harper is both.

04:36.000 --> 04:38.116
His middle name is Francis.

04:41.080 --> 04:43.071
Hi, what's going on?

04:43.240 --> 04:44.992
Trying to save you a little money here.

04:45.160 --> 04:47.720
Good man, appreciate it.

04:47.880 --> 04:50.553
Check out what I bought Linda.

04:54.120 --> 04:55.235
Diamond earrings?

04:55.400 --> 04:56.958
She's a classy woman, Alan.

04:57.120 --> 04:59.839
She's not gonna be impressed
with a continental breakfast...

05:00.000 --> 05:01.319
...and a copy of the video.

05:05.680 --> 05:09.309
Be that as it may, you can't keep
spending money you don't have.

05:09.480 --> 05:11.869
Oh, relax. Something will turn up.

05:12.040 --> 05:14.349
Will you stop saying that?
Things don't just turn up.

05:14.520 --> 05:18.035
You're living in a dream world.
Money doesn't just fall from the sky.

05:18.200 --> 05:20.350
Obviously you've never been
sitting ringside...

05:20.520 --> 05:23.080
...when a pole dancer
hangs upside down.

05:29.200 --> 05:32.556
So did you buy this for your girlfriend
because you're breaking up with her?

05:32.720 --> 05:34.438
No, why would you think that?

05:34.600 --> 05:37.956
Because you always give jewelry to girls
you're getting ready to dump.

05:38.120 --> 05:39.235
Very observant.

05:39.760 --> 05:41.910
You watch, you learn.

05:42.120 --> 05:47.433
Well, this isn't breakup jewelry,
this is "I like you, stick around" jewelry.

05:48.200 --> 05:51.078
- What's the difference?
- About 1500 bucks.

05:53.080 --> 05:55.275
But let's back up a step.

05:56.040 --> 05:58.395
A gentleman never dumps a lady.

05:58.560 --> 06:01.916
He merely acknowledges the fact
that a relationship has run its course...

06:02.080 --> 06:04.389
...by presenting her with a memento...

06:04.560 --> 06:07.313
...a keepsake if you will,
of their time together.

06:07.480 --> 06:10.119
Remember that big blond
who threw the toaster oven at you?

06:11.640 --> 06:13.073
Yeah, I remember.

06:13.240 --> 06:14.468
Oh, and that yoga teacher...

06:14.640 --> 06:17.313
...who chucked the fire extinguisher
through your windshield.

06:17.480 --> 06:18.469
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

06:18.640 --> 06:22.792
- There was that actress who set fire...
- It's not a perfect system, Jake.

06:27.320 --> 06:30.915
Oh, Charlie, they're beautiful.

06:31.760 --> 06:34.991
You do realize I was going to sleep
with you tonight anyway.

06:35.880 --> 06:37.598
This is just a little bonus.

06:37.760 --> 06:40.832
Like when you get to a baseball game
and find out it's helmet night.

06:41.320 --> 06:43.550
You silver-tongued devil.

06:43.720 --> 06:47.713
Well, I don't know about silver,
but you'll find I am tongued.

06:51.760 --> 06:55.514
If you ignore that,
there's a matching necklace in it for you.

06:56.160 --> 06:58.151
Why don't you open the wine?

07:00.600 --> 07:02.397
Gary, what are you doing here?

07:02.560 --> 07:04.869
I'm sorry, I tried to call
but your line's been busy.

07:05.040 --> 07:07.395
My line's been busy?
I haven't been on the phone.

07:07.560 --> 07:09.676
Well, I must have called 20 times.

07:09.840 --> 07:11.637
Fine. What do you want?

07:11.800 --> 07:14.473
I have to work tonight
and I can't take Brandon.

07:14.640 --> 07:17.313
- But I have company.
- And I have an emergency board meeting.

07:17.480 --> 07:19.550
- Who are you?
- I'm Charlie.

07:19.720 --> 07:20.914
I'm Brandon.

07:21.080 --> 07:22.308
Nice to meet you, Brandon.

07:23.200 --> 07:26.192
You know,
I have a nephew about your age.

07:29.640 --> 07:32.871
Hey, Dad, did you get Mom a present
when you got divorced?

07:33.040 --> 07:34.109
A present?

07:34.280 --> 07:36.748
Yeah, a memento of your time together.

07:39.280 --> 07:42.272
Jake, buddy, you're the memento
of our time together.

07:43.480 --> 07:46.438
So you were too cheap
to get her earrings.

07:47.640 --> 07:49.870
She did better than earrings.

07:50.040 --> 07:52.508
She got my family jewels.

07:53.200 --> 07:54.758
- Hi, honey.
- Hi, Mom.

07:54.920 --> 07:56.990
When you die,
do I get Dad's family jewels?

07:57.480 --> 08:00.199
- What?
- Nothing, just go inside.

08:00.360 --> 08:03.875
- Okay, well, thanks for dropping him off.
- Judith, hang on a second.

08:04.040 --> 08:05.234
What?

08:06.680 --> 08:09.319
- How's it going?
- Good.

08:09.480 --> 08:12.040
So your new marriage going well?
Herb's okay?

08:12.200 --> 08:13.519
What do you want, Alan?

08:14.640 --> 08:16.835
Charlie's business is dead,
I'm gonna be homeless.

08:17.000 --> 08:18.115
Well, you can't stay here.

08:18.680 --> 08:21.592
Oh, no, no,
that's not what I was getting at...

08:21.760 --> 08:24.877
...but it's good to know
that door is firmly closed.

08:25.040 --> 08:30.114
No, what I was hoping was that
we could talk about the child support.

08:30.280 --> 08:32.032
What about my child support?

08:32.200 --> 08:37.399
Well, technically, it's Jake's
child support, hence the term "child."

08:39.080 --> 08:41.958
But I just thought maybe
we could make some trims.

08:42.120 --> 08:45.351
For instance, the karate classes,
the archery lessons...

08:45.520 --> 08:47.238
...the algebra tutor.

08:47.400 --> 08:50.119
I mean, I don't know about you,
but I've never seen him...

08:50.280 --> 08:53.158
...you know, break a board
or string a bow.

08:53.320 --> 08:56.039
And the algebra tutor,
I mean, who are we kidding?

08:57.600 --> 09:00.239
That's like putting swim fins on a cat.

09:00.400 --> 09:03.915
He needs the tutor, he likes the lessons
and I'm not gonna ask Herb to pay.

09:04.080 --> 09:07.390
- That's okay, I'll ask him. Is he home?
- Goodbye, Alan.

09:09.640 --> 09:12.996
How about I stay in Jake's tree house?
He never uses it.

09:14.520 --> 09:17.512
Kid doesn't even like to climb stairs.

09:18.720 --> 09:20.995
Come on, sweetheart, just one little bite.

09:21.160 --> 09:22.149
Nope.

09:23.440 --> 09:25.237
He's usually not this cranky.

09:25.400 --> 09:27.914
Have you tried a little whiskey
in his sippy cup?

09:28.080 --> 09:31.436
- Charlie.
- I'm just saying, it worked for my brother.

09:31.600 --> 09:34.273
- You really did that?
- Still do it.

09:35.080 --> 09:37.514
You know what,
I'm just gonna make him a hot dog.

09:37.680 --> 09:39.398
- You want a hot dog?
- Sure.

09:40.280 --> 09:42.919
- I was talking to my son.
- What, you just got the one?

09:43.720 --> 09:45.392
I'll be right back.

09:45.560 --> 09:48.677
Come on, kid, just have a little corn
and then bedtime.

09:48.840 --> 09:51.354
- For both of us.
- No.

09:51.960 --> 09:53.598
Oh, for the love of God.

09:53.760 --> 09:57.469
I don't come to Gymboree
and knock the blocks out of your hand.

09:59.360 --> 10:01.191
Come on.

10:01.360 --> 10:04.193
It's corntastic.

10:07.240 --> 10:09.959
&lt;i>I like corn&lt;/i>
&lt;i>It tastes real sweet&lt;/i>

10:10.960 --> 10:13.633
&lt;i>I don 't like peas&lt;/i>
&lt;i>They taste like feet&lt;/i>

10:15.560 --> 10:18.916
&lt;i>Corn 's the king&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Of the veggie-food group&lt;/i>

10:19.080 --> 10:21.799
&lt;i>And it looks the same&lt;/i>
&lt;i>When it's in your poop&lt;/i>

10:24.760 --> 10:26.113
Son of a bitch.

10:27.400 --> 10:29.152
I mean, golly.

10:41.320 --> 10:42.878
Yeah.

10:43.040 --> 10:44.234
Hi, Mom.

10:44.400 --> 10:46.038
&lt;i>Hello, Alan.&lt;/i>

10:47.280 --> 10:48.429
Got a minute?

10:49.040 --> 10:50.359
&lt;i>Sure.&lt;/i>

10:55.880 --> 10:58.917
I mean, could you come to the door?

11:01.560 --> 11:02.549
&lt;i>No.&lt;/i>

11:03.480 --> 11:07.439
Please, Mom, it's important.
I'm having a real crisis here.

11:07.600 --> 11:10.592
&lt;i>Oh, darling, I'm so sorry.&lt;/i>

11:10.760 --> 11:11.909
&lt;i>Well, good luck with that.&lt;/i>

11:14.200 --> 11:15.269
Mom, please.

11:16.560 --> 11:18.596
&lt;i>I'm such a pushover.&lt;/i>

11:20.880 --> 11:25.237
The money isn't just for me.
It's for Charlie and your only grandson.

11:25.400 --> 11:27.868
I'll just be a minute, Teddy.

11:33.000 --> 11:34.752
What can I do for you, Alan?

11:38.280 --> 11:39.269
Nothing. Never mind.

11:41.960 --> 11:45.270
What? I'm not entitled to a love life?

11:47.240 --> 11:50.516
I'm ready for my punishment,
headmaster.

11:57.360 --> 12:01.148
So you must be getting tired, huh?

12:02.840 --> 12:04.558
No shame in calling it a night.

12:04.760 --> 12:06.671
I gotta go pee-pee.

12:06.840 --> 12:07.909
All right, go ahead.

12:08.080 --> 12:12.312
First pee-pee then beddy-bye.
Beats the other way around, trust me.

12:12.480 --> 12:14.516
I gotta go pee-pee now.

12:15.000 --> 12:16.877
Linda, he says he's gotta go pee-pee.

12:17.040 --> 12:19.713
- Would you mind taking him?
- Me?

12:19.880 --> 12:22.110
He can't undo his pants
and I'm doing the dishes.

12:23.560 --> 12:26.393
Fine, let's go pee-pee.

12:27.760 --> 12:28.909
Don't feel bad.

12:29.080 --> 12:31.913
I can't always undo my pants either.

12:35.560 --> 12:38.996
- What are you waiting for?
- I don't have to anymore.

12:39.160 --> 12:41.435
Linda, he says
he doesn't have to anymore.

12:41.600 --> 12:43.511
Trust me, he has to.

12:44.560 --> 12:47.996
- You heard the lady, let her rip.
- No.

12:49.640 --> 12:52.996
Okay, okay, how about this?

12:53.160 --> 12:58.439
You're a giant, and there's a tiny village
in the toilet bowl that's on fire...

12:58.600 --> 13:03.549
...and you have to put it out
by whizzing all over it.

13:03.720 --> 13:04.755
Hey, look.

13:05.200 --> 13:07.316
Here comes the giant now.

13:09.080 --> 13:12.390
&lt;i>I had a root beer&lt;/i>
&lt;i>I had a Coke&lt;/i>

13:12.560 --> 13:16.553
&lt;i>I need to pee&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Hey, I smell smoke&lt;/i>

13:16.720 --> 13:19.871
&lt;i>Giant, giant&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Up in the sky&lt;/i>

13:20.040 --> 13:24.033
&lt;i>Grab your fire hose&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Let it fly&lt;/i>

13:24.200 --> 13:26.919
&lt;i>Close your windows&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Lock your doors&lt;/i>

13:27.080 --> 13:32.200
&lt;i>Because when I rain&lt;/i>
&lt;i>It really pours&lt;/i>

13:34.240 --> 13:36.356
There you go.

13:37.080 --> 13:41.312
Hey, hey, hey, I'm the only one
who gets to pee on my feet.

13:47.360 --> 13:49.954
Come on, buddy, right in here.

13:50.120 --> 13:52.509
Hey, Berta, look what I got.

13:52.680 --> 13:56.195
Big deal. It's a freaking miracle
you don't have 10 of them.

13:57.000 --> 13:59.309
This is Linda's son, Brandon.

13:59.480 --> 14:01.072
I'm Brandon.

14:01.240 --> 14:02.639
I got ears.

14:03.600 --> 14:04.919
So, what's he doing here?

14:05.080 --> 14:06.832
- I'm babysitting.
- You?

14:07.000 --> 14:09.878
- Why not me?
- You're a rum-soaked degenerate.

14:10.720 --> 14:13.678
Yeah, but it turns out I have child skills.

14:13.840 --> 14:17.071
I already got him to eat his vegetables
and make pee-pee in the toilet.

14:17.240 --> 14:19.754
So, "Do as I say, not as I do," huh?

14:21.680 --> 14:23.159
Are you gonna help me or what?

14:23.320 --> 14:25.436
Hey, his mom's not throwing me any.

14:28.400 --> 14:29.992
Don't get the wrong idea.

14:30.160 --> 14:33.596
Your mom and I are actually
in a committed relationship.

14:36.520 --> 14:39.159
So if I sign up for this drug trial...

14:41.840 --> 14:43.432
...I take these pills not knowing...

14:43.600 --> 14:46.160
...if I'm getting the anxiety medication
or a placebo?

14:46.320 --> 14:47.435
That's correct.

14:47.600 --> 14:49.511
The test group
gets the actual medication...

14:49.680 --> 14:53.070
...and the control group
is being given sugar pills.

14:54.280 --> 14:56.111
So is there anything
I should know about?

14:56.280 --> 14:58.032
Any side effects or anything?

14:58.200 --> 15:01.317
Well, that's one of the purposes
of the research.

15:01.480 --> 15:04.756
But in tests of this nature,
common side effects include:

15:04.920 --> 15:08.833
"Dry mouth, hair loss,
blurred vision, inflamed gums."

15:09.000 --> 15:10.274
- Okay.
- " Mild nausea.

15:10.440 --> 15:12.670
Heart palpitations, liver damage.

15:13.720 --> 15:17.395
Boils, shingles, sudden fainting...

15:17.560 --> 15:21.235
...and temporary darkening of the stool."

15:23.160 --> 15:25.037
Good Lord.

15:25.200 --> 15:26.997
How much do you pay people to do this?

15:27.160 --> 15:29.355
- A thousand dollars a week.
- I'm in.

15:42.960 --> 15:44.951
Hey, hey, hey.

15:45.120 --> 15:47.111
That's not a toy.

15:47.280 --> 15:50.989
That's how I make my living. Not
so much anymore, but still, be careful.

15:51.160 --> 15:52.593
I wanna play.

15:53.120 --> 15:54.553
All right.

15:54.960 --> 15:57.076
Play this one.

15:58.880 --> 16:00.677
And this one.

16:02.880 --> 16:04.632
That's great.

16:04.800 --> 16:06.518
Now it's my turn.

16:08.680 --> 16:13.993
This is a little tune I wrote for my nephew
when he was feeling down in the dumps.

16:14.160 --> 16:18.119
&lt;i>I know that the winter&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Follows the fall&lt;/i>

16:20.120 --> 16:23.351
&lt;i>And in New York&lt;/i>
&lt;i>The buildings are tall&lt;/i>

16:26.080 --> 16:28.799
&lt;i>I hear that in China&lt;/i>
&lt;i>They have a Great Wall&lt;/i>

16:31.080 --> 16:33.833
&lt;i>I know these things and more&lt;/i>

16:34.000 --> 16:39.154
&lt;i>But there's just one answer&lt;/i>
&lt;i>I'm still looking for&lt;/i>

16:43.000 --> 16:46.197
&lt;i>Who cut the cheese?&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Who cut the cheese?&lt;/i>

16:46.360 --> 16:49.830
&lt;i>I ask you, please&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Did you cut the cheese?&lt;/i>

16:50.000 --> 16:53.231
&lt;i>I'm not averse to learnin '
&lt;i>Tell me why my eyes are burnin '

16:53.400 --> 16:55.072
&lt;i>Who cut the cheese?&lt;/i>

16:55.240 --> 16:56.468
Everybody.

16:56.640 --> 16:59.871
&lt;i>Who cut the cheese?&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Who cut the cheese?&lt;/i>

17:00.040 --> 17:03.510
&lt;i>I ask you, please&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Did you cut the cheese?&lt;/i>

17:03.680 --> 17:07.275
&lt;i>I'm not averse to learnin '
&lt;i>Tell me why my eyes are burnin '

17:07.440 --> 17:12.070
&lt;i>Who cut the cheese?&lt;/i>

17:18.240 --> 17:19.912
I can't thank you enough.

17:20.120 --> 17:22.588
No problem, we had fun.

17:23.080 --> 17:26.516
Look, after I drop him off at his dad's,
why don't I come back...

17:26.680 --> 17:29.399
...and show my appreciation
for those earrings?

17:29.560 --> 17:32.870
Gee, I'd love to, but it's been a long day.

17:33.040 --> 17:36.555
I just wanna soak in a hot bath
and have a little me time.

17:37.000 --> 17:38.877
Oh, come on, Charlie.

17:39.040 --> 17:41.474
Hey, hey, hey,
while you were off having fun at work...

17:41.640 --> 17:44.791
...I was cooped up all day in this house
taking care of your child.

17:44.960 --> 17:46.473
Okay, sorry.

17:46.640 --> 17:49.791
I'm just saying I'm not a light switch.

17:50.320 --> 17:51.799
I'll call you later.

17:52.680 --> 17:56.309
Oh, wait, wait.
I made something for Brandon.

17:58.360 --> 18:00.749
I sang some songs for him,
he seemed to like them...

18:00.920 --> 18:02.672
...so I burned them onto a CD.

18:02.840 --> 18:04.068
Oh, how sweet.

18:04.240 --> 18:07.471
Sweet?
Clearly you're not familiar with my work.

18:07.640 --> 18:09.039
Anyway, he seemed to dig them.

18:09.200 --> 18:10.997
Well, thank you.

18:14.080 --> 18:16.150
Hi, Alan.

18:16.320 --> 18:17.753
Hi.

18:34.360 --> 18:37.397
I don't think I'm in the control group.

18:55.240 --> 18:58.198
Are you really sure you should be
taking those pills with beer?

18:58.360 --> 19:01.079
What else can happen to me, Charlie?

19:01.240 --> 19:05.153
My hair is coming out,
I'm having fainting spells...

19:05.320 --> 19:08.596
...I can see my heart beating
through my shirt...

19:09.160 --> 19:11.276
...and my poop looks like
charcoal briquettes.

19:11.440 --> 19:14.512
So stop taking the medication.

19:14.680 --> 19:16.398
It's $ 1000 a week.
We need the money.

19:16.560 --> 19:18.676
Oh, relax. Something will turn up.

19:18.840 --> 19:20.671
Something's already turned up.

19:20.840 --> 19:23.718
I'm pretty sure I dropped a third testicle.

19:29.360 --> 19:30.349
Hello?

19:31.160 --> 19:32.275
Hang on.

19:32.440 --> 19:34.908
It's Linda's ex-husband.
He wants to talk to you.

19:35.080 --> 19:37.548
- I don't wanna talk to him, talk to him.
- I'm not gonna.

19:37.720 --> 19:40.109
Come on. You've got 30 percent
more balls than I do.

19:46.360 --> 19:49.796
Hello? Yeah, this is Charlie.

19:49.960 --> 19:51.632
What about Brandon?

19:52.120 --> 19:54.759
Oh, good, good,
I'm glad he likes the songs.

19:55.960 --> 19:58.997
Yeah, Linda mentioned
you were in the music business.

19:59.520 --> 20:03.877
Well, that's flattering, but I already have
a very lucrative career writing jingles.

20:04.040 --> 20:08.909
I don't see myself walking away
from that to record children's songs.

20:10.800 --> 20:12.518
How much?

20:13.040 --> 20:14.029
I'm in.

20:15.640 --> 20:17.995
How about that? Something turned up.

20:20.600 --> 20:21.999
Send the papers over.

20:22.160 --> 20:24.549
Great, great.

20:25.480 --> 20:30.759
No, no, I love kids.
And more important, they love me.

20:34.960 --> 20:36.916
No, no, no. None of my own.

21:05.120 --> 21:07.111
Subtitles by
SDI Media Group

21:07.280 --> 21:09.271
[ENGLISH]
